---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import NistPasswordPolicy from '../../components/NistPasswordPolicy';
---

<Layout title="NIST-Compliant Password Policy Generator" description="Generate a modern, copy-pasteable password policy based on the latest NIST guidelines.">
  <div class="bg-indigo-50 py-12 border-b border-indigo-100">
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 text-center">
      <h1 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-extrabold text-indigo-900 tracking-tight mb-4">
        NIST Password Policy Generator
      </h1>
      <p class="text-lg text-indigo-800">
        Stop forcing your employees to change their passwords every 90 days. Generate a modern, secure policy based on the latest National Institute of Standards and Technology (NIST) guidelines.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="max-w-7xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 py-12">
    <NistPasswordPolicy client:load />

    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto mt-12 bg-white border border-slate-200 p-8 rounded-2xl shadow-sm">
      <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-900 mb-4">Why upgrade your password policy?</h3>
      <p class="text-slate-600 mb-4">
        For decades, IT departments forced employees to create complex passwords (like <code>P@ssw0rd1!</code>) and change them every 90 days. The National Institute of Standards and Technology (NIST) recently updated their official guidelines (SP 800-63B) because <strong>these old rules actually make security worse.</strong>
      </p>
      
      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-6 mt-8">
        <div class="bg-red-50 border-l-4 border-red-500 p-4 rounded-r-lg">
          <h4 class="font-bold text-red-900 mb-2">The Old Way (Bad)</h4>
          <ul class="space-y-2 text-red-800 text-sm">
            <li>• Require a mix of upper, lower, numbers, and symbols.</li>
            <li>• Force users to change passwords every 90 days.</li>
            <li>• Result: Employees write passwords on sticky notes, or just change <code>Spring2023!</code> to <code>Summer2023!</code>.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        
        <div class="bg-emerald-50 border-l-4 border-emerald-500 p-4 rounded-r-lg">
          <h4 class="font-bold text-emerald-900 mb-2">The NIST Way (Good)</h4>
          <ul class="space-y-2 text-emerald-800 text-sm">
            <li>• Require long "passphrases" (12+ characters).</li>
            <li>• Never force password expirations unless there is a known breach.</li>
            <li>• Screen new passwords against known breached lists.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>
